WEBVTT

00:00:00.294 --> 00:00:01.008
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:01.762 --> 00:00:03.699
Sheryl and Dharmesh

00:00:04.778 --> 00:00:08.116
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> But soon after the couple got married in 1992,

00:00:08.282 --> 00:00:14.103
they began to realize their food differences were too big to be fixed by a spoon.

00:00:14.802 --> 00:00:18.919
Dharmesh was training to be a dentist whilst Sheryl stayed at home,

00:00:19.053 --> 00:00:20.857
so she did all the cooking.

00:00:20.992 --> 00:00:25.633
<v><b>Sheryl:</b></v> My simple, you know, chicken and potatoes, basic foods and – that was interesting,

00:00:25.633 --> 00:00:30.676
because he would put masala and anything hot and spicy on top of it that he could find.

00:00:31.001 --> 00:00:34.530
I felt a little bit insulted, like, you know,

00:00:34.529 --> 00:00:38.032
you can understand cultural differences in your head,

00:00:38.032 --> 00:00:40.155
but in your heart it’s, it’s hard to accept.

00:00:40.155 --> 00:00:43.053
I felt, like, ‘Wow, he doesn’t like my cooking!’

00:00:43.299 --> 00:00:46.272
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> And, Dharmesh, what were you thinking at the time?

00:00:46.272 --> 00:00:49.782
Were you enjoying this food that Sheryl was making? Be honest.

00:00:50.695 --> 00:00:53.954
<v><b>Dharmesh:</b></v> Er, it was very bland, honestly.

00:00:56.152 --> 00:00:56.911
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:57.292 --> 00:00:59.232
Rebecca and Saj

00:01:00.056 --> 00:01:03.364
<v><b>Rebecca:</b></v> When I see anyone eat meat, but in particular Saj,

00:01:03.364 --> 00:01:06.549
it’s a thing that’s quite hard to describe to people who aren’t vegan.

00:01:06.549 --> 00:01:10.010
It’s not just nauseating and kind of a little bit gross,

00:01:10.035 --> 00:01:12.673
it’s also something, kind of, profoundly hurtful,

00:01:12.951 --> 00:01:16.330
so it’s even worse watching someone that you love doing that

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.848
and I think that’s where the tolerance has to come from.

00:01:18.948 --> 00:01:22.944
<v><b>Saj:</b></v> My favourite meaty meal is a chicken teriyaki.

00:01:22.945 --> 00:01:26.175
Like, that’s the thing that I really hanker for.

00:01:26.421 --> 00:01:32.052
So, if I’m finishing work, I walk past this Japanese restaurant

00:01:32.313 --> 00:01:35.159
and they’ve got just this most amazing chicken teriyaki.

00:01:35.254 --> 00:01:37.480
<v><b>Emily:</b></v> Do you tell Rebecca about it when you get home?

00:01:37.814 --> 00:01:40.601
<v><b>Saj:</b></v> Um, no I – I usually don’t.

00:01:40.728 --> 00:01:43.349
Just depends on how brave I’m feeling.